  With the travel command:

    - Using capital letters moves the cursor by ten spaces 
      instead of one.  (It should move ten in the horizontal
      direction and three in the vertical direction.)

    - Pressing the key for a character symbolizing a specific
      terrain object like "<>_#" etc. cycles the cursor through
      objects of that type. 

      - If you want to travel to a point near a terrain object,
        move the cursor there first, then use the normal 
        direction keys to fine tune your destination.


  The travel command is highly recommended for those with 
teleportitis.  Especially as once you get teleport control
the keys work the same way for choosing your teleport location.


  

